  <data name="TextBox1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step 0) Connect your HC05 to an FTDI type device like the pictures on the right. There are too many combinations of boards and FTDI type boards. you will need to be able to wireup your hardware.
*Be careful to use the proper voltages. some HC 05 chips are stickly 3.3 volts, some are 5volts. same goes with the FTDI boards.  

Usage: connect hardware to PC before opening the program. Select and Com port and connect to the FTDI (or similar) device.  

The left side is fore reading 7 basic settings that most users are interested in.

The right side has a check bock to select Read or Write Mode. Select a command in read mode and click "Send Read Command". If in write mode you must select a command and also enter
the CORRECT PARAMATERS for that command. the Parameters are found in the HC 05 datasheet.

TLDR:
Make Sure Key/EN PIN is HELD high (3.3v or 5 volts depending on hardware)
Connect to Serial Port
Click Read button on left bottom
Click checkbox to switch to Write mode.
Read again to see if command was saved</value>
